CXR_VQA_RESULT={"status": "completed", "observation": {"answer": "Yes, there are significant lung opacities, consolidations, and likely pleural effusions visible in this chest X-ray.\n\nSpecifically:\n\n*   **Right Lung:** The right lung appears significantly more opaque than the left lung. There is a diffuse pattern of increased density, which could represent consolidation, edema, or other infiltrative processes. The upper right lung appears particularly affected.\n*   **Left Lung:** The left lung also shows some increased density, but to a lesser extent than the right. This could be due to edema, pneumonia, or other infiltrative processes.\n*   **Pleural Effusions:** There is blunting of the costophrenic angles on both sides, which is suggestive of pleural effusions. The effusions are likely bilateral, with the right side appearing more prominent.\n\nThe overall appearance is concerning for a significant pulmonary process, possibly pneumonia, ARDS, or other inflammatory/infectious conditions. Further evaluation with CT imaging would be necessary to characterize the specific nature and extent of the abnormalities.\n\nIt is important to note that this is a preliminary interpretation based on a single image. A complete assessment requires correlation with the patient's clinical history, physical examination findings, and other relevant investigations.", "model": "google/medgemma-4b-it", "revision": "290cda5eeccbee130f987c4ad74a59ae6f196408", "backend_input_tokens": 299, "backend_output_tokens": 251}, "derived_images": [], "backend_compute_seconds": 20.76826926996, "cuda_peak_allocated_bytes_by_visible_device": [9942664192], "original_image": "../../../assets/2929f6ea130ef608aaa5616836b699bcd382469680d0d5a5902222fd9d56bb45.jpg", "raw_result_file": "[REDACTED]", "clinical_correctness_verified": false, "actual_model_events": [{"kind": "generate", "model_class": "Gemma3ForConditionalGeneration", "module": "transformers.models.gemma3.modeling_gemma3", "status": "completed